Implement src/explore-plots.ts: approved Explore SU2 linked graphics only.
Conventions: docs/plans/rust-physics-platform/game-exploration/README.md (repo root).
Export interface PlotSnapshot {coordinates:[number,number,number,number];alpha:[number,number];beta:[number,number];stereographic:{status:'finite'|'pole';point:number[]|null};slice:{coordinate:number;radius:number|null;status:'sphere'|'point'|'empty'};bloch:number[]}.
Export mountPlots(host:HTMLElement):{update(snapshot:PlotSnapshot):void;dispose():void}.
MUST take all mathematical values from Rust; no group, norm, stereographic, slice-radius or Bloch computations. Graphics geometry and camera transforms allowed. alpha=a0+i a3; beta=a2+i a1. Plot linked complex planes with numeric axes, unit references and selected diamonds. Chart x=(a1,a2,a3)/(1-a0), missing pole I; explicit finite/invalid/pole readouts and labeled fit extent for large coordinates. No sign canonicalization: U and -U stay distinct.
Slice a0=c: supplied radius sqrt(1-c²), bounded 3D wireframe sphere; point at supplied radius zero, empty without geometry. Selected point shown only within display tolerance |a0-c|<=1e-7. Explicit off-slice label. Distinguish SU2≈S³, coordinate slice and supplied Bloch S² vector. No normalization or silent mathematical corrections.
Dependency-free Canvas2D orthographic 3D prototype with truthful label. Bounded 11 circles×65 samples, DPR≤2. Shared camera, drag with pointer capture/cancellation, arrows and Home, keyboard orbit/reset buttons. No inertia or animation, reduced-motion safe. Responsive cards, inherited theme colors/fonts, inline scoped layout only; no style.css edits. Accessible DOM numeric readouts independent of canvas, no color-only identification. Resize/theme redraw and complete teardown of observers/listeners/pointer capture/owned DOM; idempotent dispose and harmless post-disposal updates. Copy caller snapshot arrays. No downloads/dependencies or other repository edits.
Validate strict TypeScript using /tmp/mathphysics-workbench/node_modules and temporary staging. Independently exercise finite/pole, slice sphere/point/empty/off-slice, keyboard/drag/reset, themes/resize and lifecycle. This manual unit does not claim automated PDD regeneration or application integration.

Integration: parent Snapshot extends PlotSnapshot and passes the whole snapshot to update. Parent owns abort/request status. Expose .plot-card, .plot-canvas, .plot-readout for parent CSS. Empty Rust slice status MUST produce visible text matching /empty|no slice/i. Preserve chart equations and accessible numeric vectors.

Layout integration: inner root MUST explicitly set inline grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) so inherited .explore-plots two-column rules cannot split headings/readouts/card-grid into columns. Keep responsive columns solely on the nested card grid. Parent owns host layout. Existing slider and camera interactions suffice; complex-plane clicks do not alter mathematical parameters.

Rust pole status can include numerical chart limits: readout MUST say pole/off-chart without asserting the selected state is exactly I. Keep I identified separately as the mathematical excluded pole in the chart equation. Camera interactions MUST NOT mutate mathematical snapshot state or caller data.
